<article class="env-lemma" id="03BW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03BW">Lemma <span data-tag="03BW">66.4.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $X = U/R$ be a presentation of $X$, see Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/0263" data-tag="0263">65.9.3</a>. Then the image of $|R| \to |U| \times |U|$ is an equivalence relation and $|X|$ is the quotient of $|U|$ by this equivalence relation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The assumption means that $U$ is a scheme, $p : U \to X$ is a surjective, étale morphism, $R = U \times _ X U$ is a scheme and defines an étale equivalence relation on $U$ such that $X = U/R$ as sheaves. By Lemma <a href="/tag/03H5" data-tag="03H5">66.4.4</a> we see that $|U| \to |X|$ is surjective. By Lemma <a href="/tag/03H4" data-tag="03H4">66.4.3</a> the map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  |R| \longrightarrow |U| \times _{|X|} |U|  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is surjective. Hence the image of $|R| \to |U| \times |U|$ is exactly the set of pairs $(u_1, u_2) \in |U| \times |U|$ such that $u_1$ and $u_2$ have the same image in $|X|$. Combining these two statements we get the result of the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>